      "boundaries": [
        {
          "case": "empty",
          "status": "checked",
          "evidence": "For T=∅, W_∅={1} and C_∅={0}; its down-set consists only of the empty face and that vertex. If S=∅, then W, WS, Σ and K each have one point, all gluing/action/quotient assertions reduce to that point, and the point stabilizer is {1} (steps 1.1, 3.1, 5.2, 6.2, 7.1)."
        },
        {
