        {
          "id": "derivation-3.1",
          "step": "3.1",
          "claim": "For every vertex $v$, inclusion $j\\colon\\Sigma^2\\hookrightarrow\\Sigma$ induces an isomorphism $j_*\\colon\\pi_1(\\Sigma^2,v)\\to\\pi_1(\\Sigma,v)$.",
          "inputs": [
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.1",
            "F6",
            "given"
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "derivation-3.2",
          "step": "3.2",
          "claim": "The graph $\\Sigma^1$ is connected because its vertices are $W$ and $S$ generates $W$; every point of $\\Sigma$ lies in a convex cell containing a vertex, so $\\Sigma$ is path-connected. For any loop $\\alpha$ at $x$, a path $p$ from $x$ to $1$ makes $\\bar p*\\alpha*p$ a based loop at $1$, which Steps 1.1 and 2.2 contract. Prepending $p$ and appending $\\bar p$ gives a homotopy rel $x$ from $(p*\\bar p)*\\alpha*(p*\\bar p)$ to $p*\\bar p$; the explicit piecewise homotopy $G(u,t)=p(2u(1-t))$ for $u\\le1/2$ and $G(u,t)=p(2(1-u)(1-t))$ for $u\\ge1/2$ contracts each $p*\\bar p$, so $\\alpha$ is null-homotopic and every $\\pi_1(\\Sigma,x)$ is trivial.",
          "inputs": [
            "F1",
            "F7",
            "step 1.1",
            "step 2.2",
            "F6",
            "given"
          ]
        },
        {
